      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find out how many albums are in either Andrew's or John's collection, but not both, we can use the principle of inclusion and exclusion.\n\nLet A be the set of albums in Andrew's collection, and B be the set of albums in John's collection.\n\nWe are given:\n|A| = 17 (Andrew's collection)\n|B| = 6 + 9 (John's collection, which includes 6 albums that are not in Andrew's collection)\n|A ∩ B| = 9 (they share 9 albums)\n\nWe want to find |A ∪ B| - |A ∩ B|, which represents the number of albums that are in either Andrew's or John's collection, but not both.\n\nUsing the principle of inclusion and exclusion, we have:\n\n|A ∪ B| = |A| + |B| - |A ∩ B|\n|A ∪ B| = 17 + (6 + 9) - 9\n|A ∪ B| = 17 + 15 - 9\n|A ∪ B| = 22\n\nNow, we need to find |A ∪ B| - |A ∩ B|:\n\n|A ∪ B| - |A ∩ B| = 22 - 9\n|A ∪ B| - |A ∩ B| = 13\n\nSo, there are 13 albums in either Andrew's or John's collection, but not both.",
